From bdd3251b927cbb512105f9d56ade15a8c68bd48c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joshua Strobl <me@joshuastrobl.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 18:02:09 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(budgie-menu): focus search entry when opened via
 keybinding

During the move to Wayland, our Budgie Popovers were converted from being Gtk.Window to GtkPopover.
On Wayland, popovers are considered a subsurface of its parent (in our case the panel), which only
gets keyboard input while the panel itself is focused, and a keybinding can't focus the panel.

Super_L showed the menu but typing went to the previous window, so you'd have to click into the search input to start typing.

Made the menu its own toplevel layer-shell window again, this time with some custom positioning against the launcher.

I have tested it against all panel positions as well as doc mode.

Menu no longer registers with PopoverManager for obvious reasons.

Closes #842

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5-1
Signed-off-by: Joshua Strobl <me@joshuastrobl.com>
